  "question": {
    "text": "If the functions are defined as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then what is the common domain of the following functions: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#177;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></math>"
  },
  "options": [
